WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.470
Music is playing.

2
00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:03.630
A big file is downloading.

3
00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:05.590
And you're typing an essay.

4
00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:08.470
All three seem to be
running at the same time.

5
00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:11.650
But this laptop has just one CPU core.

6
00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:14.950
And one core runs one
instruction at a time.

7
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.130
So how can one core keep three apps going?

8
00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:21.010
In this mission, you'll
meet the operating system:

9
00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:24.550
the manager that sits between
your apps and the hardware.

10
00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:26.870
Apps don't control the
hardware themselves.

11
00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:30.730
They ask the OS, and it
manages the hardware for them.

12
00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:33.690
You'll find that each
running program is a process,

13
00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:36.650
and every process needs the processor.

14
00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:41.040
Your mission: explain how one
core can run three apps at once.
